Carlos plants the lemon tree for $90, which is a one-time cost. Each year, he sells 7 lemons at $1.50 each, generating revenue of \(7 \times 1.50 = \$10.50\). Additionally, he incurs annual costs of $3.00 for watering and feeding. Therefore, his net profit per year (after annual costs) is \(10.50 - 3.00 = \$7.50\).

