- Cumulative revenue after 12 years: \(12 \times 10.50 = \$126.00\)
- Cumulative costs after 12 years: \(90 + (12 \times 3) = 90 + 36 = \$126.00\)
- Profit: \(126.00 - 126.00 = \$0.00\)

After 13 years, he begins earning money:
- Cumulative revenue: \(13 \times 10.50 = \$136.50\)
- Cumulative costs: \(90 + (13 \times 3) = 90 + 39 = \$129.00\)
- Profit: \(136.50 - 129.00 = \$7.50\)

Thus, it takes 13 years for Carolyn to start earning money on her lemon tree.

