\]

The required speed for the remaining distance is:
\[
\text{Speed} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Time}} = \frac{6}{1} = 6 \text{ miles per hour}
\]

Thus, Marissa needs to walk the remaining distance at 6 miles per hour to achieve an average speed of 4 miles per hour.

