There are 36 months, and the increase occurs every two months, so the number of two-month periods is \(36 \div 2 = 18\).  

The total increase over 18 periods is \(18 \times 4 = \$72\).  

The final price is the original price plus the total increase: \(20 + 72 = \$92\).  

Since the increase is based on the original price each time, it is not compounded.  

Thus, after 36 months, a bag of marbles costs $92.  
