- Team A scored \(\frac{1}{4}\) of Team B's second-half goals, so \(\frac{1}{4} \times 8 = 2\) goals.  

Total goals:  
- First half: Team A (4) + Team B (2) = 6 goals  
- Second half: Team A (2) + Team B (8) = 10 goals  
- Overall total: \(6 + 10 = 16\) goals  

