The school auditorium has 4 rows of seats, with 18 seats in each row, so the total number of seats is \(4 \times 18 = 72\).

One-fourth of the seats were occupied by administrators: \(\frac{1}{4} \times 72 = 18\) seats.

The remaining seats after administrators are occupied are \(72 - 18 = 54\).

One-third of these remaining seats were occupied by parents: \(\frac{1}{3} \times 54 = 18\) seats.

The rest of the seats were occupied by students, which is two-thirds of the remaining seats: \(\frac{2}{3} \times 54 = 36\) seats.

Alternatively, since students occupy two-thirds of the seats after administrators, and administrators occupy one-fourth of the total, students occupy \(\frac{2}{3} \times \frac{3}{4} = \frac{1}{2}\) of the total seats: \(\frac{1}{2} \times 72 = 36\) seats.

Thus, there were 36 students in the school auditorium.

