This is a linear growth problem. I should find the growth rate per year.

Growth per year = total growth / number of years = 8 inches / 4 years = 2 inches per year.

Now, for 13 years, growth = growth per year × number of years = 2 inches/year × 13 years.

Calculate that: 2 × 13 = 26 inches.

